  <title>Fullscreen session</title>

<p>Fullscreen mode lets <app>Pano Terminal</app> use the entire screen. It
  hides the header bar, so that you can see more lines.</p>

  <p>To enter fullscreen mode, press <key>F11</key>, or press the menu button
  in the top-right corner of the window and select
  <gui style="menuitem">Full Screen</gui>.</p>

  <p>To leave it, press <key>F11</key> again, or right-click the terminal and
  select <gui style="menuitem">Leave Full Screen</gui>.</p>

  <note style="tip">
    <p>If you have more than one tab open, the tabs stay visible in
    fullscreen mode.</p>
  </note>

